1
00:05:16,363 --> 00:05:22,363
Time heals the heart. Faith heals the rest.

2
00:10:32,727 --> 00:10:38,727
Diary of a Mad Black Woman is a drama, romance,
comedy film directed by Darren Grant.

3
00:15:49,090 --> 00:15:55,090
Charles, an attorney, and Helen, his devoted wife, seem to have
everything – money, a beautiful mansion – the American Dream.

4
00:21:05,454 --> 00:21:11,454
However, as Helen prepares to celebrate their 18th wedding anniversary, her life takes an unexpected twist
when she comes home to find her clothes packed up in a U-Haul van parked in the driveway.

5
00:26:21,818 --> 00:26:27,818
Charles is divorcing her and kicks her out.

6
00:31:38,181 --> 00:31:44,181
Helen moves in with her grandmother Madea, an old woman
who doesn't take any lip from anyone.

7
00:36:54,545 --> 00:37:00,545
Madea helps Helen through these tough times by showing
her what is really important in life.

8
00:42:10,909 --> 00:42:16,909
Helen is forced to rediscover love, life, and
religion in her pursuit for happiness.

9
00:47:27,272 --> 00:47:33,272
Helen McCarter, played by Kimberly Elise.

10
00:52:43,636 --> 00:52:49,636
Charles McCarter, played by Steve Harris.

11
00:58:00,000 --> 00:58:06,000
Madea / Brian / Joe, played by Tyler Perry.

12
01:03:16,363 --> 01:03:22,363
Orlando, played by Shemar Moore.

13
01:08:32,727 --> 01:08:38,727
Brenda, played by Lisa Marcos.

14
01:13:49,090 --> 01:13:55,090
Debrah, played by Tamara Taylor.

15
01:19:05,454 --> 01:19:11,454
Diary of a Mad Black Woman is a 2005 American romantic comedy drama
film directed by Darren Grant and written by Tyler Perry.

16
01:24:21,818 --> 01:24:27,818
Inspired by the play of the same name, it marks Perry's feature film
debut and is the first entry in the Madea film franchise.

17
01:29:38,181 --> 01:29:44,181
Starring Perry alongside Kimberly Elise, Steve Harris, Shemar Moore, and Cicely Tyson, it tells the story of a woman who is thrown out of her house by her
husband on their 18th wedding anniversary and subsequently moves in with her grandmother, and is the only film written, but not directed, by Perry.

18
01:34:54,545 --> 01:35:00,545
Filmed in Atlanta and Fairburn, Georgia, and released theatrically by Lionsgate Films
on February 25, 2005, the film grossed $50.6 million in North America.

19
01:40:10,909 --> 01:40:16,909
The sequel, Madea's Family Reunion, was released on February 24, 2006.

20
01:45:27,272 --> 01:45:33,272
The film explores themes of new love, faith,
forgiveness, crooked lawyer, revenge.

21
01:50:43,636 --> 01:50:49,636
The tone is lighthearted and emotional and mind_bending.
